# aurora.local / packages/filebrowser/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/filebrowser/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/filebrowser/pins.env to adopt.
#
# Every pin below is curated and human-reviewed.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# filebrowser/filebrowser — IMPORTANT PROJECT-STATUS FINDING: File
# Browser (the original project) is winding down. Its GitHub releases
# page states the last planned release has shipped and the repository
# will be archived on 2026-09-01 — after that, no further releases, bug
# fixes, or security fixes, ever. compose.yml currently pins v2.31.2,
# already many releases behind. The final release is v2.63.23, verified
# to exist and match `:latest` today.
#
# Judgement call: v2.31.2 -> v2.63.23 is a big jump (thirty-plus point
# releases) within the same major version, not a documented breaking
# change, but also not something this task tested end to end — the
# operator should read the intervening changelog and test config/data
# compatibility before adopting it, rather than trust this pin blindly.
# The alternative is to stay on v2.31.2 (known-working, but will never
# receive another security fix from upstream either way, since the
# whole project stops). A maintained fork, "FileBrowser Quantum"
# (gtsteffaniak/filebrowser), exists as a successor but is a different
# image/config surface — a separate decision, not made here.
#
# Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed for
# both v2.31.2 and v2.63.23. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_FILEBROWSER=filebrowser/filebrowser:v2.63.23@sha256:a469ea076d4a1b4b1d86a41d130f2f536cd9da996a2b1fb39c0d7635f9d89b9a
